See [[http://mightyohm.com/blog/2008/10/building-a-wifi-radio-part-3-hacking-the-asus-wl-520gu/|MightyOhm's discussion]].

Pinout: Pin 1 (white bar on silkscreen): 3.3V; Pin 2: RX; Pin 3: TX; Pin 4: GND.\\

If you're using GNU screen and a [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial#usb.to.rs232.ttl.converter.module|USB-serial adapter]], the command will look something like this (OSX):

  screen /dev/tty.SLAB_USBtoUART 115200,-parenb,-cstopb,cs8

On other OSes, you'll need to change the path to the USB-serial device.

